# CASE with GROUP BY

Example:

```sql
SELECT
CASE
    WHEN salary < 50000 THEN 'Low'
    ELSE 'High'
END AS salary_group,
COUNT(*) AS total
FROM Employee
GROUP BY
CASE
    WHEN salary < 50000 THEN 'Low'
    ELSE 'High'
END;
```

---

# CASE inside ORDER BY

Custom sorting:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Orders
ORDER BY
CASE
    WHEN status='approved' THEN 1
    WHEN status='pending' THEN 2
    ELSE 3
END;
```

Output order:

```
approved
pending
rejected
```

